    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for E.164 telephone numbers in the owner-create flow.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the single telephone validation point, used by `POST /api/owners`):\n\n- Added a `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS` map declaring the required national-digit count per country code (`+61` \u2192 9, `+1` \u2192 10).\n- Extended `normalizeTelephone(...)` so that, after a number passes the existing E.164 syntactic pattern (`+` followed by 8\u201315 digits), it also checks the national-number length via the new `hasValidNationalNumberLength(...)` helper. A wrong length for a known country code returns `null`, which the controller already turns into a **400 Bad Request**. Country codes with no listed rule are left unaffected (still bounded by the 8\u201315 digit pattern).\n\nThis keeps the existing design intact: `normalizeTelephone` remains the one place that decides validity, and the controller's existing `if (telephone == null) \u2192 BAD_REQUEST` branch handles rejection. The new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` (posting `+61 123`, which normalizes to `+61123` with only 3 national digits) is rejected, and the valid unique AU numbers (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 `+61` + 9 digits) still pass. Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures.",
